this is going to pay a perf penalty in a lot of cases.  maybe something like

```
if array_equivalent(a, b, strict_nan=True):
    # GH#66699 [reasoning for these extra checks]
    if a.dtype.kind in "iu" and b.dtype.kind == "f":
        int_arr = a
    elif a.dtype.kind == "f" and b.dtype.kind in "iu":
        int_arr = b
    else:
        return True
     if not int_arr.size or np.abs(int_arr.astype("f8")).max() <= 2**53:
         return True
```

Skips should be done on test collection, not test execution, where ever possible. Use

    @td.skip_if_no("pyarrow", min_version="24.0")

instead.
